# Hint text

Put one short fact under a label or legend when most people need it before they answer. Say what the value is for, what format it takes or what it will change.

## When to use it

Use a hint for a unit, a format or a consequence. For example, “How long the light stays on after movement” under a duration field. An option can have its own hint when its label is not enough.

Write about what the person wants to do, not about the system. Use “Bedside lamp” rather than `light.bedside_lamp`. Name the entity ID only when the task is advanced configuration. If a value changes only what is displayed, say so. If it changes an automation, say that instead.

## When not to use it

Do not put a manual, a link, a details control or a safety instruction in a hint. Move long help into the page, outside the described-by text. A placeholder is not a hint because it disappears when the person starts typing.

## How it behaves

Place the hint after the label or legend and before the field. Link it to the field with `aria-describedby`. Keep any error ID in the same attribute when validation fails, so a screen reader reads the label, hint and error together. A short hint keeps that output short.

